+# Internal HTTP Policy
+
+Plain HTTP is permitted for communication between internal-only services: the architecture requires TLS (via the project's Rustls backend) only at the perimeter for external-facing connections, while trusted internal host-to-host traffic may use unencrypted HTTP to reduce TLS overhead, accepting a deliberate security/performance trade-off for paths that never leave the internal network.
